{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00276",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.53,
      "end_seconds": 4.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Hi there, is it alright if I come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.88,
      "end_seconds": 9.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "You're fine, sit down. So, what brings you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 9.62,
      "end_seconds": 13.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.85,
      "end_seconds": 16.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 17.52,
      "end_seconds": 20.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "We came because of my heart racing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.6,
      "end_seconds": 23.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.31,
      "end_seconds": 37.93,
      "duration_seconds": 12.62,
      "text": "Um, it's been two months, I'm fairly sure. I did try to ignore it for a while. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.34,
      "end_seconds": 40.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.18,
      "end_seconds": 49.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Moderate, I'd say. I've also had shaky hands, since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.38,
      "end_seconds": 52.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Have you been feeling anxious and jittery?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.33,
      "end_seconds": 63.34,
      "duration_seconds": 10.01,
      "text": "So, you know, yeah. Two days, I'd say. I've been losing weight even though I'm eating well too, since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.56,
      "end_seconds": 79.68,
      "duration_seconds": 15.12,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.09,
      "end_seconds": 82.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.59,
      "end_seconds": 85.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Has there been any diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.16,
      "end_seconds": 88.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Not at all, no diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 88.99,
      "end_seconds": 94.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "Right, actually, doctor, I did notice diarrhoea. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.42,
      "end_seconds": 101.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.91,
      "end_seconds": 110.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.78,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any trouble sleeping, lump in the neck or shortness of breath at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.08,
      "end_seconds": 116.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "No, no trouble sleeping, lump in the neck or shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.05,
      "end_seconds": 119.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.27,
      "end_seconds": 123.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "I mean, no, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.76,
      "end_seconds": 126.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.38,
      "end_seconds": 129.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "My mother has migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.56,
      "end_seconds": 144.06,
      "duration_seconds": 14.5,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.11,
      "end_seconds": 150.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.99,
      "end_seconds": 154.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Right, any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.82,
      "end_seconds": 174.85,
      "duration_seconds": 19.03,
      "text": "Okay, uh, so I've got low haemoglobin. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. Yeah, uh, yes, depression. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.95,
      "end_seconds": 181.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Okay, low haemoglobin, that's already on your record. Good to know. Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.47,
      "end_seconds": 191.2,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "Just a hernia repair, about five years back. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.84,
      "end_seconds": 196.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.53,
      "end_seconds": 198.42,
      "duration_seconds": 0.89,
      "text": "No allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.13,
      "end_seconds": 200.06,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.24,
      "end_seconds": 204.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "I stopped smoking about two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.25,
      "end_seconds": 211.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.72,
      "end_seconds": 215.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Sertraline. I take it 50 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 216.62,
      "end_seconds": 224.3,
      "duration_seconds": 7.68,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the sertraline was 100 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.34,
      "end_seconds": 228.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.43,
      "end_seconds": 232.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "No, um, I left it at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.54,
      "end_seconds": 238.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.33,
      "end_seconds": 255.11,
      "duration_seconds": 15.78,
      "text": "For the most part, you know, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.87,
      "end_seconds": 258.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Okay, I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.03,
      "end_seconds": 269.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.3,
      "end_seconds": 292.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 106, temp 36.6 degrees, saturation 98 percent. And pressure 135 over 70."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.16,
      "end_seconds": 294.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.74,
      "end_seconds": 298.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.85,
      "end_seconds": 305.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.97,
      "end_seconds": 306.67,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.07,
      "end_seconds": 310.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.41,
      "end_seconds": 326.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "There's a fine tremor in the outstretched hands, and your palms are warm and moist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.44,
      "end_seconds": 331.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.87,
      "end_seconds": 352.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Your thyroid feels a little enlarged and smooth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.12,
      "end_seconds": 367.29,
      "duration_seconds": 9.17,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It fits best with an overactive thyroid. I'd also keep a heart rhythm problem in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.27,
      "end_seconds": 373.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Okay, so I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.85,
      "end_seconds": 390.54,
      "duration_seconds": 15.69,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an overactive thyroid, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had your heart racing for two months, moderate, and no lump in the neck."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 391.03,
      "end_seconds": 392.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.63,
      "end_seconds": 397.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Sorry about the noise outside, the building work never stops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.99,
      "end_seconds": 400.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "I hadn't even noticed, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.98,
      "end_seconds": 403.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "I'm going to order an ECG, for palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.02,
      "end_seconds": 406.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.63,
      "end_seconds": 426.32,
      "duration_seconds": 19.69,
      "text": "We should do a thyroid test for hyperthyroid symptoms. I'd like to arrange a thyroid scan for hyperthyroidism. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. Let's use propranolol, 20 milligrams, twice a day, until we review. That's for palpitations and tremor. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 427.71,
      "end_seconds": 430.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Alright, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 431.74,
      "end_seconds": 450.48,
      "duration_seconds": 18.74,
      "text": "Limit tea, coffee and anything that speeds up the heart for now. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. I'll also refer you to an endocrinologist. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 451.67,
      "end_seconds": 453.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 456.62,
      "end_seconds": 462.8,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 464.21,
      "end_seconds": 464.91,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 466.3,
      "end_seconds": 477.29,
      "duration_seconds": 10.99,
      "text": "Please come and see me after the results are back. Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 478.13,
      "end_seconds": 487.1,
      "duration_seconds": 8.97,
      "text": "So, I take the propranolol, 20 milligrams, twice a day and come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 488.58,
      "end_seconds": 493.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we've covered it. Do you have any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 493.92,
      "end_seconds": 498.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Right, I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    }
  ]
}